# Normalize line endings: LF in the repository and in the working tree, so the
# ruff formatter (line-ending = "lf" in ruff.toml) and Windows checkouts stop
# rewriting each other's files. Matches MAST_common's .gitattributes.
#
# This repo is Windows-only, but nothing in it wants CRLF: there are no tracked
# .bat/.cmd/.ps1/.sh files, and Python on Windows is newline-agnostic. The blobs
# were already LF (core.autocrlf=true has been converting on commit all along) --
# only the checkout was CRLF, and that mismatch was what made `ruff format`
# condemn every file in the repo.
#
# The vendored-SDK rules below deliberately override this line; keep them last.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored greateyes SDK — keep exactly as the vendor shipped it.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the MAST machines, which would rewrite the wrapper's
# CRLF endings to LF in the blob and break byte-for-byte comparison against the
# upstream archive. `-text` disables EOL conversion so the sha256 recorded in
# cameras/greateyes/sdk/VENDOR.md verifies directly against a fresh checkout.
cameras/greateyes/sdk/greateyesSDK.py -text

# The SDK DLL must never be touched by EOL or diff heuristics.
cameras/greateyes/sdk/lib/** binary
